 "name": "snow_lair_broken",
 "description": "Same footprint, layers and hole as snow_lair_cutaway but the roof has caved in: jagged hole through the top of the drift (x about -70..130) open into the cave, broken snow chunks on the cave floor, a puff of snow, cave empty. Cross-section of a ringed-seal birth lair. Anchor (0,0) = snow surface level at the centre; snowdrift mound top y -160; cut face of drift and snow layer #e6eef5 with faint layer lines (snow layer y 0..140); cave hollow #cfe2ee x -220..260, y -60..140 (floor = sea-ice top); sea-ice band #bcd3e3 y 140..260 with a dark breathing hole x 120..200 open to the water below. Side edges unoutlined so the shot's background bands (surface y 0, ice 140..260, water #3a9ad9 below) continue. ~840x420 (x -420..420, y -160..260).",
